 "note": "an oscillator is made when the clock starts the node and compared with X_ITE 16.6.0 while running: wave type (default square; SINE, TRIANGLE, SAWTOOTH and CUSTOM from a PeriodicWave), frequency held at 0 or more, detune, and the source's output gain. A second start builds a new oscillator with the current settings. Runs on the real clock. Signal compared with X_ITE 16.6.0 on the page's real Web Audio clock (a tap on the node's output). SINE gives rms 0.7071 and a pure 440 Hz, TRIANGLE rms 0.5774 with odd harmonics 8/(pi k)^2, CUSTOM from optionsReal/optionsImag matches the normalised harmonics computed from the coefficients; the default SQUARE and SAWTOOTH are compared with the browser's own OscillatorNode of the same type (Web Audio's band limited waves are peak normalised: rms 0.843 and 0.485, not the ideal 1 and 0.577) and keep the harmonic ratios 1/3 (square) and 1/2, 1/3 (sawtooth); frequency, detune (+-1200 cents = an octave), gain, stop (silent after the 30 ms fade), restart, pause and resume are measured the same way. Each number is held to the analytic value or the reference and to X_ITE.",
